{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1407759-true-fae-and-sever-oaths","id":1407759,"title":"True Fae and Sever Oaths","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-12T13:19:51-07:00","id":1407759,"title":"True Fae and Sever Oaths","content":"<i>&quot;Any Title can make a bargain by swearing upon the Fae\u2019s true Name. Fae bargains work differently than changeling bargains do. Both parties must agree to perform a task, give up a possession, abide by a rule, or something equally concrete and clearly communicated. For the True Fae, the consequences for failing to uphold its end is permanent destruction.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Connecting the two leads some to assume that an Adept of Fate can royally and lethally inconvenience a True Fae simply by locking them into a re-worded bargain containing cheated conditions that weren't originally in-place. Except just how reasonable is this? The Gentry are effectively gods, both metaphorically and literally. Would you allow it? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23821-rathford","name":"Rathford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23821_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T13:44:59-07:00","id":1407768,"title":"","content":"Considering the various &quot;This spell does not affect Rank 6+ entities&quot; clauses for many spells, you might simply not be able to cast such spells in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T13:48:23-07:00","id":1407771,"title":"","content":"<i>&quot;Since Gentry pledges have such dire consequences when broken, the Fae don\u2019t make them often or lightly. Convincing one of the Good Cousins to make a pledge is difficult at best and usually requires a changeling to set up an untenable situation for it first.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> With that following paragraph in mind, I'm not sure it's necessarily a big deal. You're talking about a powerful sorcerer personally meeting one of the incarnated Titles of the True Fae, manuevering them into striking a bargain that they're already very averse to making, and then casting against what might possibly be a 6+ Withstand, against a character with a power list of &quot;arbitrarily any power that might fit as a Contract within X Regalia.&quot;<br /> <br /> The True Fae probably are loathe to personally deal with enchanters on the path of thorns for both this reason and others, which in turn makes it harder to pull off.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T15:12:53-07:00","id":1407802,"title":"","content":"While the rule for Rank 6+ ones is currently left ambiguous, nothing would prevent them from using a Veiling of Fate to hide the terms of the oath, to word them in such a way that makes breaking them seem correct to the True Fae and their agents.<br /> <br /> Another option is that it would require conjunctional Mind, following the train of thought from the Dark Eras spells.<br /> <br /> Lastly, perhaps the True Fae is Rank 6+, but the Rank of the embodied Title is not. In this way, it would be all about impossible to do this within their own Arcadian manses (at least not without thoroughly researching them first), but it would be possible to do so everywhere else, with the difficulty being modified by the Rank of the manifested Title, similar to spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T01:21:33-07:00","id":1407877,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure a true Fey's titles are all bolstered by the presence of multiple titles &quot;Each of a True Fae\u2019s Titles has a Wyrd rating of 5, plus one dot for each Title the Fae possesses (including this one), to a maximum of 10.&quot;<br /> <br /> That said, &quot;true&quot; rank 6 entities I do not believe refers to such as a rank 6 spirit exceeds stats and game rules, while a wyrd 6 true fey has a single title and is on the scale of a changeling (1-10) and very much with in the realm of stats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T09:59:50-07:00","id":1408181,"title":"","content":"Perhaps the Wyrd itself could protect oaths and vows from True Fae, it isn't a force likely to forget a promise even if a Mage changes one, not either without archmastery or something.<br /> <br /> Conversely just make it a clash of wills?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}